eighty Yojanas.","alignment":{"type":"approximate","confidence":0.13,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-65-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4064009","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"68d654471d1540ba605c431f42f9d562639523fc57300f7f576e701c55dcbdb5","compact":"ccae3e9e7cfe722dda596eaaf88a31c53970256deeb9bc61a3be70b1c61bce22","nasal":"ccae3e9e7cfe722dda596eaaf88a31c53970256deeb9bc61a3be70b1c61bce22"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-64-10","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":64,"verse":10,"english":"As they were speaking thus,' the oldest of them all, Jambavān, saluting them answered.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-65-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4064010","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2c691f0f21cc7b9cd2de51a9fc64b1fd82bee4711c8a4934b965a51a6924b627","compact":"18177905def9f235a5d167eab0798321b18661878c61c17556ccac37f505149c","nasal":"43cf9f49a4f07aea4ccf2b5ac29bf193c3c484149dfb02d6a1624cebb9750ebe"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-64-11","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":64,"verse":11,"english":"Formerly we had power of motion. But now we have waxed exceeding old. Although this is so, yet we can not overlook this, as both Rama and the monkey-king (by sending us) have become sure of success. At present do you understand the course that is ours. I shall go ninety Yojanas. There is no doubt whatever about this.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-65-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4064011","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2822ef096b03f457bb3d92ff29a3fa4db80d829ae7966aa68bef0cf9dc5f70a4","compact":"9deef7434d2834ccaac21d2912e92d17b5430e937ee9368fa5ec8cbd8d56ad15","nasal":"e1