erly) my prowess in leaping was forsooth not such.* Of old in the sacrifice of Virocana's son, the external Lord Visnu, when he had covered the entire universe with three steps, was circumambulated by me. *i.e. it was greater.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.829,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-65-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4064014","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e544bb42907be670496b8fd23a7e8687209b2efd31be1bba72070f11146e9eb4","compact":"cdff033a2312b6f3bff9ed2d5c0cba4ec2f720df1e1b8a75a668a8a9b831154e","nasal":"4379df6d7e806b49316922ae16bdcaf44d427432810b395440c65081a801bc01"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-64-15","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":64,"verse":15,"english":"Jāmbavān said this to those choice monkeys. But (formerly) my prowess in leaping was forsooth not such.* Of old in the sacrifice of Virocana's son, the external Lord Visnu, when he had covered the entire universe with three steps, was circumambulated by me. *i.e. it was greater.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.708,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-65-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4064015","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c4c660dd7e776d978189cdf739c20543b740dae86c24713c2456170e55fc2b66","compact":"b2df2c8e02e9470f508f69c5f2798dad4219a86fa52158ebfc285d19ba78a088","nasal":"b2df2c8e02e9470f508f69c5f2798dad4219a86fa52158ebfc285d19ba78a088"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-64-16","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":64,"verse":16,"english":"But I who was all this, have waxed old, and my vigour sits feebly upon me. In my youth, ever, my strength was exceeding great and incomparable.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.963,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-65-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4064016","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1c6a6684929ab36a07c392fde8c40c6c7516a16102a3961e79ed88a749f7bacb","compact":"a83ce4e62246103f478aab2ee2ddd79f410a6c5af1053656feb51ee8d45e092c","nasal":"6aaf91bf39ac6b8c98569d686aeef39df18803da598c128a0cd8379fdeeb3db2"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-64-17","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":64,"verse":17,"english":"Now I can only by my own energy, course thus far. But has a bound shall not bring success on our undertaking.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.493,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-65-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4064017","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"383c250ca8f6a1c7304c3d8fe6e467c1e7cb814284640b996a34f9bef0eadbb4","compact":"09d8f7969ea16941fb9390cfa44d86b7a3c4c27c623140520b0af2e63976c0d6","nasal":"09d8f7969ea16941fb9390cfa44d86b7a3c4c27c623140520b0af2e63976c0d6"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-64-18","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":64,"verse":18,"english":"After this, saluting the mighty monkey, Jāmbavān, the wise Angada spoke straight sense, saying,","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.823,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-65-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4064018","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ab2fa771d40a0525647338f5aaec06490a984803d67235867433c3342e303659","compact":"0379a74af86f0ff32dc837303809310a64ad465ccab701a6159e5212c4c1e7c6","nasal":"01a2dbe536ffea5974970c833cec8b12671ade138cc86f7bd73e87326267d337"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-64-19","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":64,"verse":19,"english":"I can go over this mighty hundred Yojanas; but there is no certainty as to my answer of returning.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.873,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-65-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4064019","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e946eb0702f3d3fe20a53d711381ae766a861a111b2bba3c24fe3c00deb6de75","compact":"b7192c1474b7533c8fd642d9c20a7e09d6e2d09f1b15215388c33327edb208ec","nasal":"a823dde9d205744333674bf14aea86b927c92c5289dbdf1f888fa35690fe75e6"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-64-20","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":64,"verse":20,"english":"Thereat, Jāmbavān, cognizant of speech, said to that foremost of monkeys,-0 foremost of leonine as, we know your power of motion, you are capable of ursing a hundred thousand Yojanas, as well as of coming back. But we say that even this is what is fit.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.492,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-65-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4064020","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"90bbf647e638e0532e69401ced0221772e8ea345061cd6f3928b2c5923f814b0","compact":"c6d58c2c6432d34738266910752a495f71ed233913398a7a2590c4e0066eb3c7","nasal":"a596deba6aab526ed13c0ff33d92f4c4e75e33809ca76a7bd56de516094d7dc8"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-64-21","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":64,"verse":21,"english":"Thereat, Jāmbavān, cognizant of speech, said to that foremost of monkeys,-0 foremost of leonine as, we know your power of motion, you are capable of ursing a hundred thousand Yojanas, as well as of coming back. But we say that even this is what is fit.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.859,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-65-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4064021","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3fedcf4ffac185598730a8b038b09199a2307ace8ff62c0fb6a380a1dabc2b56","compact":"b1256959f3a4e43d183b5144c3725512f870ddfdcb17974acc848b0f206d671e","nasal":"ff96e71ce4a834632a3c9321a70aadef6cf1f0196600491cec5f8b12bc2dad4b"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-64-22","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":64,"verse":22,"english":"My child, ore master must on no account be commanded by his servants. foremost of monkeys, all these should be commanded your you.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.879,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-65-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4064022","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6d7dc9f9dcd7c387ac2344116ed42cfdde6e9fc6e3da5aac817465a709fee230","compact":"319f97f5ad92858af1a4d15cc0d6aec6b9b951665a99ffe094aa49d98bd71117","nasal":"319f97f5ad92858af1a4d15cc0d6aec6b9b951665a99ffe094aa49d98bd71117"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-64-23","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":64,"verse":23,"english":"You are our spouse, and (at the same time) occuying the position of our husband. The master is the spouse if the army. This is the way of the world.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.871,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-65-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4064023","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f75bbc51c367e81faf689171161c426229cc197c59df2658aca5563ec7c854b4","compact":"d50b7878147e8fc1ad2a185dfc8d7ea68079d9915db25acc51de7b98bd04e7a3","nasal":"d50b7878147e8fc1ad2a185dfc8d7ea68079d9915db25acc51de7b98bd04e7a3"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-64-24","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":64,"verse":24,"english":"O repressor of oes! O subduer of enemies, you are the root of this business. Therefore, my child, you should always be maintained by us like a wife.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.82,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-65-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4064024","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c92a2d0212612468676c5bf02f9fc7d04d504531a8ff61eadd80a08ceaf48d63","compact":"fc5df6bb21eec36e33697368e03abb7fd619a4599fcb109b6deb9d147699cb69","nasal":"fc5df6bb21eec36e33697368e03abb7fd619a4599fcb109b6deb9d147699cb69"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-64-25","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":64,"verse":25,"english":"The root of any work must be preserved. This is the policy of those versed in business. The root existing, all the virtues, obtaining fruit, certainly meet with success.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.689,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-65-21"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4064025","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2c42692e258a1187c94e02c5e0fac55131625f3bafd0ca833759ca2969829faa","compact":"94d6f50fa6dc22adc3ecafbb5780b15f362b0f7e87abf2788d470d76cfe7a7aa","nasal":"96ef2cf5eb03a7d9c1b0da70e17bd274e81209b8f8fc1f386d64a7cc941182c4"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-64-26","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":64,"verse":26,"english":"You, O you having truth for prowess are the instrument of this undertaking, and, O subduer of enemies, furnished with sense and vigour, you are the occasion herein. And, O foremost of monkeys, you are both our superior, and our superior's son; and resorting to you we are enabled to accomplish our object.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.459,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-65-22"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4064026","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4adec0cfb2c7eedd87cedd3cb2d67e40840b892714dc4eeffa1f2b9904ebbc45","compact":"209262acd893f72929790cf63a6d430395b23e767c4e499cea799b7dcb832f0b","nasal":"89fb7eb1e2b85641a7d51d42fd0970a5ee709f806c5cb02567144f8ec83273dd"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-64-27","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":64,"verse":27,"english":"You, O you having truth for prowess are the instrument of this undertaking, and, O subduer of enemies, furnished with sense and vigour, you are the occasion herein. And, O foremost of monkeys, you are both our superior, and our superior's son; and resorting to you we are enabled to accomplish our object.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.887,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-65-22"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4064027","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"14f332d96b0587b61033fabcac0596cfe9a9226374b59de02372a58fb95ac0ea","compact":"b7e1164a0760024204accb451a2f26b46e039e50a4e5063ab586460c438ad18b","nasal":"8e799fba277a8d0626e107522a4611c1c96a0d72bf8178ecf25eee35aeb9e3cd"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-64-28","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":64,"verse":28,"english":"Threat that mighty monkey, Angada, son to Vali, answered the exceedingly wise Jambavan, when he had spoken,","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-65-23"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4064028","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"07aee70ce6e0731f3e63173eab755987956b81bad5bdbfe355a26fbbdb449584","compact":"7808acf35e1509738e1daae430f1b417b1762aa4d037ad43eab4f58b4ac90e0a","nasal":"a272104101c3ba716863483445a67829d8c8a3d5324b744bc9ad8c50652bdb7c"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-64-29","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":64,"verse":29,"english":"If I go not, nor any other powerful monkey, then we should for certain again sit ourselves down to fast to death.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.742,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-65-24"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4064029","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f8d27ba0f350a75e24f1b1944a76c2c0ccf5bacb97fd09e617c7bb6ab1c48664","compact":"3be3b2a3c819dd3f09b79afe2fdc855a846c6ee57d44a1231baadd6bfcb6f708","nasal":"3be3b2a3c819dd3f09b79afe2fdc855a846c6ee